# MDB Production-first workflow

**Production** (`https://www.digitalmusicdatabase.com`) is the **primary acceptance environment** for completed features.

## Release sequence

1. Develop and complete the feature in the repo.
2. Run **relevant automated verify scripts** (`scripts/verify-*.mjs`, package `verify:*`).
3. Review **migrations and RLS/security** before any Production apply.
4. Review **changed files**; do not bundle unrelated WIP.
5. **Deploy** completed, verified commits to **Production** (not Preview-only sign-off).
6. **Verify live Production** (HTTP/API + owner browser when needed).
7. Test **desktop, iPhone Safari, and Android Chrome** (and Capacitor if the feature touches store builds).
8. Report deployment SHA, probes, and **remaining issues**.

## Staging / Preview

- Staging (`jzlegcbotqfzevtczwhx`) and Vercel Preview remain for **isolated development and experiments**.
- Do **not** treat staging catalog data as Production truth; cross-platform acceptance must use **the same Production URL** on all devices.
- **Do not** require duplicate full-matrix testing on Preview when Production verification has passed for the shipped SHA.

## Safety (non-negotiable)

- Preserve **beta payment locks** (ringtone, subscriptions, sales checkout).
- **No** real charges, payouts, or enabling paid checkout for general users unless owner explicitly changes env for launch.
- **No** accidental publication of private/draft content; no copying staging rows into Production to “fake” visibility.
- Maintain **rollback** (redeploy prior Production SHA).
- **Never** deploy unfinished or unverified work to Production.

## Current priority

Complete **Production ringtone download** acceptance (published catalog row on Production + free acquisition + Android/iPhone download), then continue creator/listener features under this workflow.